 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Zariski's Main Theorem as a factorization",
 "statement": "Let $f\\colon X\\to Y$ be separated, quasi-compact, locally quasi-finite and\nlocally of finite type. Then $f$ factors as\n\n$$\nX\\xrightarrow{\\;j\\;}W\\xrightarrow{\\;g\\;}Y,\\qquad g\\circ j=f,\n$$\n\nwith $j$ an open immersion and $g$ an affine morphism.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-prop-nagata-sketch-zmt/lemma-nagata-zmt-open-immersion-affine-factorization.md",
  "place": "node lemma-nagata-zmt-open-immersion-affine-factorization, order 183"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "This is Grothendieck's form of Zariski's Main Theorem, available in Mathlib\nas `Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/ZariskisMainTheorem.lean`. Take $W$ to\nbe the relative normalization of $Y$ in $X$, $j$ the canonical morphism\n$X\\to W$ and $g$ the structure morphism $W\\to Y$. Zariski's Main Theorem\nsays that $j$ is an open immersion under exactly these hypotheses, and $g$ is\nintegral, hence affine, by construction of the relative normalization.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
